// Communities (DEC-075): a cohort dimension beside age band and income class.
// Every neighbourhood holds age × class cohorts for each community, so an
// expansion can add an Indigenous nation, an immigrant community, or a
// linguistic minority here without code. The base pack ships one community,
// which costs nothing. Registry order is load order (files by path, then item
// order).
//
// Exactly one community omits `share`: it takes each neighbourhood's
// remainder. Every other community has a share model:
//   "share": { "base": 0.0, "by_neighborhood": { "rural": 0.12 }, "regional_sd": 0.05 }
// Its share of each age × class group in a neighbourhood is base +
// by_neighborhood[kind] + a regional offset (one draw per region, sd
// regional_sd), clamped to [0, 1]; shares adding up to more than 1 are scaled
// down. Optional fields:
//   "attitude_offsets": { "localism": 0.3 }  added to seeded attitudes, by key
//   "turnout_offset": -0.08                  added to seeded turnout
//   "immigration_share": 0.0                 share of international immigrants
{
  "kind": "communities",
  "items": [
    { "id": "community.general", "name_key": "community-general" },
  ],
}
